        "comment_created_at": "2026-10-11T05:27:24+00:00",
        "comment_author": "roboomp",
        "comment_body": "**should-fix \u2014 `bun install` does not fail when a dependency's lifecycle script is untrusted.** The PR body says a future script-required dependency will make installation fail loudly, but Bun skips that script and completes the install; `bun pm untrusted` already lists four blocked packages here, while CI's install step (`.github/actions/bun-install/action.yml:114`) checks only the exit code. A newly added native dependency that needs postinstall can therefore pass CI and fail at runtime. Please correct that claimed failure mode; maintainer should decide whether warning-only enforcement is acceptable or a failing check is needed.",
        "pr_file_module": null
      },
